<%- include("partials/header.ejs") %>

<div class="about-page">

    <section class="about-hero">
        <span class="about-label">ABOUT SONARA</span>
        <h1>Discover music.<br>Explore Sonara.</h1>
        <p> Sonara is a music discovery website built to make exploring
            artists, albums, songs, genres, and music from around the
            world simple and enjoyable.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span>01</span>
            <h2>What is Sonara?</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-content">
            <p> Sonara is a music exploration platform where you can
                search for and discover music in one place.
            </p>
            <p> Instead of focusing only on individual songs, Sonara
                lets you explore music through different paths, including
                artists, albums, genres, and countries.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- features -->
    <section class="about-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span>02</span>
            <h2>Explore music your way</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="features-grid">
            <article class="feature-card">
                <span class="feature-number">01</span>
                <h3>Artists</h3>
                <p> Discover artists and explore the music associated
                    with them.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
                <span class="feature-number">02</span>
                <h3>Albums</h3>
                <p> Explore albums and see the songs and information
                    connected to them.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
                <span class="feature-number">03</span>
                <h3>Songs</h3>
                <p> Find individual tracks and listen to available
                    previews.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
                <span class="feature-number">04</span>
                <h3>Genres</h3>
                <p> Explore music through different genres and discover
                    something new.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
                <span class="feature-number">05</span>
                <h3>Countries</h3>
                <p> Explore music through different countries and
                    discover artists from around the world.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="feature-card">
                <span class="feature-number">06</span>
                <h3>Search</h3>
                <p> Quickly search for the music, artists, albums, or
                    songs you're looking for.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- how it works -->
    <section class="about-section">

        <div class="section-heading">
            <span>03</span>
            <h2>How Sonara works</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-content">
            <p> Sonara uses music catalog information and promotional
                content made available through Apple's iTunes Search API
                to help users discover music.
            </p>
            <p> The information returned by the API is used to display
                things such as artist names, album information, song
                information, artwork, and available previews.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- why i built it -->
    <section class="about-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span>04</span>
            <h2>Why I built Sonara</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-content">
            <p> Sonara was created as a project to explore music,
                web development, and the process of building a complete
                music discovery experience from the ground up.
            </p>
            <p> The goal is to keep music discovery simple while making
                it fun to explore beyond the music you already know.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- technology -->
    <section class="about-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span>05</span>
            <h2>Built with</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="technology-list">
            <span>HTML</span>
            <span>CSS</span>
            <span>JavaScript</span>
            <span>EJS</span>
            <span>Node.js</span>
            <span>Express</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- legal -->
    <section class="about-section legal-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span>06</span>
            <h2>Music &amp; artwork</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-content">
            <p> Sonara uses promotional music content and artwork made
                available through Apple's iTunes Search API to help users
                discover the associated music.
            </p>
            <p> Song previews are provided courtesy of iTunes and are
                intended for promotional music discovery purposes.
            </p>
            <p class="legal-note">
                Apple and iTunes are trademarks of Apple Inc. Sonara is
                not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Apple.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
    
</div>

<%- include("partials/footer.ejs") %>